# UST.G3EU component-16 evidence

This directory contains the small, Git-suitable proof interface for the exact
component-16 adjudication.

## Tracked evidence

- `H02.component16.omitted_rows.*` selects the 38 rows outside the exact
  rank-1,200 subsystem.
- `H02.component16.exact_audit_rows.*` partitions the selected subsystem into
  800 recovery-enforced rows and a 400-row literal audit complement.
- `H02.component16.residual_mod_p*_g*.nmr` records fresh denominator-safe
  specializations of the omitted-row residual map.
- `H02.component16.modular_residual_campaign.json` independently checks every
  finite witness and records only the rigorous characteristic-zero lower
  bound.
- `H02.component16.exact_residual_rank_certificate.json` supplies the exact
  upper bound using a nonzero pivot determinant and a literal row-span
  identity over `Q(gamma)`.

## Calculation-capsule payloads

The recovered `1221 x 21 x 6` rational archive and the uncompressed exact
residual map can be several gigabytes. They are intentionally excluded from
ordinary Git history. Their paths, byte sizes and SHA-256 identities are bound
by the G3ET/G3EU certificates. A release capsule should publish those payloads
alongside the source matrix and native helper build metadata.

The finite witnesses are discovery and lower-bound tools. Repeated equal rank
at several primes is never used as an exact upper bound. Promotion occurs only
after the exact number-field row-span verifier passes.
